 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Accounts & passkeys
+
+Sign-up, sign-in and the account settings page (`/account`) support
+[passkeys](https://passkeys.dev) alongside the existing username/password flow:
+
+- **Sign up** with a passkey only (no password is ever created) or with a
+  password, after which you are offered a passkey.
+- **Sign in** with a passkey via the dedicated button or straight from the
+  username field's autofill suggestions (conditional UI).
+- **Account settings** lists your passkeys with their provider, sync/backup
+  status and last use, and lets you add, rename and remove them.
+- **Reauthentication**: removing a passkey requires having proved your
+  identity within the last 5 minutes. If not, you are asked to confirm with a
+  passkey or your password first.
+
+Passwords are still verified by the external DevTools Times API; this app only
+mirrors the username locally so passkeys can be attached to it. Accounts and
+credentials are stored in `data/passkeys.json` (override with
+`PASSKEY_DB_PATH`). The WebAuthn relying party ID and origin are derived from
+the request (honouring `X-Forwarded-Host` / `X-Forwarded-Proto`) and can be
+pinned with `PASSKEY_RP_ID` and `PASSKEY_ORIGIN`.
+
+Note that browsers only expose passkeys on `localhost` or over HTTPS.
